mpty.","The union satisfies $A\\cup B=A$.","Some element belongs to both $A$ and $B$.","The two sets are equal, $A=B$."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3835ce7aecfb95f7d4838133","time_limit":40},{"id":"subset_new_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For $\\{1,2,3\\}$, which is the correct relationship of the object $1$ to the set?","options":["$1\\in\\{1,2,3\\}$: $1$ is an element, not a subset","$1\\subseteq\\{1,2,3\\}$: $1$ appears among the listed entries","Both $1\\in\\{1,2,3\\}$ and $1\\subseteq\\{1,2,3\\}$, as they mean the same","Neither: $1$ is a number, so it cannot relate to a set at all"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"4611184fa4aadd9e83c74271","time_limit":35},{"id":"subset_new_020","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $A=\\{x\\in\\mathbb{R}\\colon x^2=1\\}$ and $B=\\{-1,0,1\\}$. Which statement is true?","options":["$B\\subseteq A$","$A\\subseteq B$","$A=B$","$A\\cap B=\\varnothing$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"c3fe08281e5318147ebedd87","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_subset_b056f914_005_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $A$ be any set. Which statement about $A\\subseteq A$ is correct?","options":["$A\\subseteq A$ holds for every set $A$.","$A\\subseteq A$ never holds, since $A$ is not smaller than itself.","$A\\subseteq A$ holds only when $A$ is nonempty.","$A\\subseteq A$ holds, so $A$ is a proper subset of itself."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"119452c828c21c46ef72fd37","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_subset_b056f914_006_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $A$, $B$, $C$ be sets with $A\\subseteq B$. Which additional assumption guarantees $A\\subseteq C$?","options":["$B\\subseteq C$","$C\\subseteq B$","$C\\subseteq A$","$B$ and $C$ have an element in common"],"answer_mode":"server","feedb